sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-04> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "A simple 2D cellular automaton (a cell turns black when exactly three of its eight neighbors are black, otherwise unchanged) can grow patterns whose overall shapes keep changing with no simple form, so complexity can appear in a pattern's overall shape as well as in its interior.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "2D cellular automata can produce complex overall shapes, not just complex interiors";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 5, “Two Dimensions and Beyond”; section “Cellular Automata” (from p. 170), p. 176. Scope: two-dimensional growth-type cellular automata"
}
